WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.770
Central Australia.

2
00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:05.810
Uluru rises, steep-sided,
from a flat plain.

3
00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:10.090
Geographers call an isolated
rock hill like this an inselberg.

4
00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:11.890
Now North Africa.

5
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:18.150
From 11,000 to 5,000 years ago, the
Sahara had vegetation and permanent lakes.

6
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.730
Those wet conditions reached as
far north as 31 degrees north.

7
00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:27.010
So why do today's deserts hold landforms
that their dry climate could never have

8
00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:27.820
made?

9
00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:31.490
In this mission, you'll
meet five dryland landforms,

10
00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:35.010
from inselbergs and pediments
to nivation hollows.

11
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:38.070
Then you'll judge how
much today's flash floods,

12
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:40.570
wind and weathering have changed them.

13
00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:45.470
Your mission: explain why deserts hold
landforms that today's dry climate could

14
00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.680
never have made.
